        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 90-year-old male patient, admitted on 22 April 2009 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed markedly reduced air entry bilaterally with expiratory wheeze, use of accessory muscles, and oxygen saturation of 84% on room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia and pneumothorax. Blood tests showed mild elevation of inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 23 April 2009 in a stable condition. Discharge medications and follow-up arrangements have been provided. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
